.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLAB-EXPORTER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm klab-exporter
.Nd serve the lab's goldens, test runs, microVMs and pool health to Prometheus
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
serves Prometheus metrics on port 9101 of every address, at
.Pa /metrics
and
.Pa / ;
any other path is 404.
Every scrape reads the state afresh from ZFS, libvirt, kfire and the lab's
results directory; nothing runs in the guests.
It serves:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Goldens
.Ql klab_golden_ready ,
.Ql klab_golden_size_bytes
and
.Ql klab_golden_info
for each of centos, rocky, fedora, debian, ubuntu and rhel: ready when
.Ar pool Ns Pa /vms/klab-golden- Ns Ar distro Ns Pa @golden
exists, with the kernel and ZFS versions read from that golden's build
log; and
.Ql klab_goldens_ready_total .
.It Lab machines
.Ql klab_site_vm_running
for the blue and green sites and
.Ql klab_test_vm_running ,
from
.Xr virsh 1 .
.It Test runs
.Ql klab_test_pass_total ,
.Ql klab_test_fail_total
and
.Ql klab_test_skip_total
for the latest run: from each distribution's summary once the run has
written one, and counted from its log while it runs; with
.Ql klab_test_status
and the test last seen.
.It Firecracker microVMs
The libvirt exporter's own series \(em
.Ql libvirt_domain_info_state ,
CPU time, memory, block and network counters \(em for every
.Xr kfire 8
instance, with the same label values, so that a microVM appears as one
more domain on the estate dashboards.
.It The pool
.Ql klab_zfs_pool_*
for size, use, health, compression, fragmentation and a one-second
.Ql zpool iostat
sample;
.Ql klab_zfs_arc_*
from the ARC kstat; used and referenced space for the pool's root, boot
and virtual-machine datasets; and snapshot counts under
.Ar pool Ns Pa /vms .
.It The host
Processor count, memory, and whether an NVIDIA device is present.
.El
.Pp
A command that fails leaves its series out and logs one line to standard
error, which the unit sends to the journal; an absent golden or virtual
machine is the normal case and is not logged.
Every label value read from a file is escaped, since one bad line fails
the whole scrape.
.Pp
.Pa klab-exporter.service
runs it as root on a KVM host, restarting it if it exits.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print its description and exit 0, serving nothing.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev POOL
The pool to report on; default
.Ql rpool .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /root/kzfs-test/
The lab's results, or
.Pa /root/klab/
when only the old one exists:
.Pa goldens/ Ns Ar distro Ns Pa -latest.log ,
and
.Pa latest ,
a link to the current run's directory holding
.Ar distro Ns Pa .summary ,
.Pa .status
and
.Pa .log .
.It Pa /var/lib/kfire/instances/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /instance.json
Each microVM; a directory without one is not counted.
.It Pa /proc/spl/kstat/zfs/arcstats , Pa /proc/spl/kstat/zfs/dmu_tx
The ARC and transaction counters.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
It serves until stopped.
It exits 1, with a Python traceback ending
.Dq Address already in use ,
if the port is taken.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, with five lab goldens built:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9101/metrics | grep -E '^klab_golden'
klab_golden_ready{distro="centos",kernel="5.14.0-741.el9.x86_64",zfs="zfs-2.2.11-1"} 1
klab_golden_size_bytes{distro="centos"} 2585702400
klab_golden_info{distro="centos",kernel="5.14.0-741.el9.x86_64",zfs="zfs-2.2.11-1",size="2585702400"} 1
\&...
klab_golden_ready{distro="ubuntu",kernel="6.8.0-138-generic",zfs="zfs-2.2.2-0ubuntu9.5"} 1
klab_golden_size_bytes{distro="ubuntu"} 1338851328
klab_golden_info{distro="ubuntu",kernel="6.8.0-138-generic",zfs="zfs-2.2.2-0ubuntu9.5",size="1338851328"} 1
klab_golden_ready{distro="rhel",kernel="",zfs=""} 0
klab_goldens_ready_total 5
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
The pool and the ARC:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9101/metrics | grep -E '^klab_zfs_(pool_healthy|pool_free_bytes|arc_hit_ratio)'
klab_zfs_pool_free_bytes{pool="rpool"} 160092041216
klab_zfs_pool_healthy{pool="rpool"} 1
klab_zfs_arc_hit_ratio 0.9981
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
Any other path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\en' http://127.0.0.1:9101/nothing
404
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kfire 8 ,
.Xr kfire-exporter 8 ,
.Xr klab 8 ,
.Xr kzfs-test 8 ,
.Xr zpool-scrub-exporter 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-08-16 the lab moved its results from
.Pa /root/klab
to
.Pa /root/kzfs-test ,
and every per-distribution test count went blank until
.Nm
looked there too.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: a quote in a run's status file made
.Xr promtool 1
reject the whole page, since the labels were not escaped; and the length
it sent counted characters, not bytes, so a test name with an accented
letter cut the end off every scrape.
Both were shown against a copy serving invented results.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
It listens on every address with no authentication; what it serves is
state, not secrets, but the lab's layout is visible to anyone who can
reach port 9101.
.Pp
Two names do not say what they hold:
.Ql klab_zfs_arc_evict_total
is the ARC's
.Ql evict_l2_eligible ,
bytes, and
.Ql klab_zfs_txg_synced_total
is
.Ql dmu_tx_assigned ,
transactions assigned rather than groups synced.
They keep their names because dashboards query them.
.Pp
Each scrape takes at least a second, for the
.Ql zpool iostat
sample, and scrapes are answered one at a time.
